    "items": [
      {
        "id": "lem-rpm-ll-reduced-ode",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Reduced-order Landau–Lifshitz local ODE and mass shell",
        "statement": "Let $(A,V,\\eta,C^+)$ be an oriented, time-oriented affine Minkowski space of dimension four with signature $(-,+,+,+)$, and fix an inertial chart $(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$ with $x^0=ct$, $c>0$. Let $O\\subseteq A$ be open and let $F$ be a $C^2$ alternating covariant two-tensor on $O$. In this chart write $F^a{}_b:=\\eta^{ac}F_{cb}$ and let $\\partial_b$ denote the coordinate partial derivative. Fix constants $\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R$ and $\\tau_e\\geq0$. For every $U\\in V$, define\n\n$$\\Pi_U{}^a{}_b:=\\delta^a_b+\\frac{U^aU_b}{c^2},\\qquad f_0^a(x,U):=\\alpha F^a{}_b(x)U^b,$$\n\n$$B^a(x,U):=\\alpha(\\partial_bF^a{}_c)(x)U^bU^c +\\alpha^2F^a{}_b(x)F^b{}_c(x)U^c, \\qquad a_{\\rm LL}^a(x,U):=f_0^a(x,U)+\\tau_e\\Pi_U{}^a{}_bB^b(x,U).$$\n\nFor the physical interpretation, $x^a$ are in metres, $\\tau$ is in seconds, $c$ is in metres per second, $U$ is in metres per second, $\\alpha=q/m$, and $\\tau_e$ is a time. Here a **proper-time parameter** means that the parameter is measured in seconds and the four-velocity is normalized by $\\eta(U,U)=-c^2$; define the future unit shell by $\\mathcal S^+:=\\{U\\in C^+:\\eta(U,U)=-c^2\\}$. For each initial datum $(x_0,U_0)\\in O\\times V$ with $U_0\\in\\mathcal S^+$, the system\n\n$$\\frac{dx^a}{d\\tau}=U^a,\\qquad \\frac{dU^a}{d\\tau}=a_{\\rm LL}^a(x,U),\\qquad (x(0),U(0))=(x_0,U_0)$$\n\nhas a unique local solution on an open proper-time interval about $0$. Along that interval $\\eta(U,U)=-c^2$ and $U$ remains future directed. This is a local ODE statement: it makes no claim of global existence for arbitrary $F$.",
        "deps": [
          "def-sr-affine-minkowski-model",
          "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
          "def-time-orientation-and-future-causal-sets",
          "def-directional-and-partial-derivatives",
          "cor-mean-value-theorem",
